A||N||5||Angela||How to uninstall/install Fiero side windows!||||9||
Z||000000||Angela||06-22-2000||04:19 AM||||Could someone please tell me or give me some instructions/tips on side window replacement.<BR> I tried to remove one off of another fiero , well I got all of the tracks and screws ect... out but there are plastic like pegs mounted on the bottom of the glass obstructing it from coming out! any clue on what to do?<BR> <BR>||||reg||9
Z||000001||BAM-BAM||06-22-2000||07:37 AM||||   I believe the way this goes is, you need to drill the center rivets out using a 1/4" drill bit.  when reinstalling the glass you can either, re-rivet the rollers or use standard bolts with associated hardware(nylox nuts) which is probably quicker if you do not have the rivetting tools. I'm sure you'll get more ideas from other members so be patient. Welcome to the greatest Fiero place on earth  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/BURNOUT.gif">     <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/lickout.gif">  <P> Late, BAM OUT!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><BR>||||reg||10
Z||000002||TOM||06-22-2000||10:59 AM||||yep thats dead on. You need to drill the rivets holding the stuff to the glass then bolt it back on once the glass in back inside the door.||||reg||1
Z||000003||tgowens||06-22-2000||12:16 PM||||Hi Angela, welcome to the forum... <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/pip7.gif"> ...those guys know what they are talkin about too, that's the way the glass is replaced. --- ||||reg||1
Z||000004||lennyb4||06-22-2000||12:49 PM||||Hey!!!! If you decide to use small bolts w/nylon lock nuts be very CAREFUL not to overtighten. I made that mistake on my camaro last summer and ended up shattering the glass.||||reg||1
Z||000005||PAUL88GT||06-22-2000||12:58 PM||||You got to love someone named Angela who can change a car window.||||reg||1
